A||N||8||Stan86SE||Stumbling, Stalling||||5||
Z||000000||Stan86SE||02-26-2001||09:43 PM||||<BR>Hi. I've got an '86 SE, 2.8L V6, Auto, with 101,000 miles.  I'm experiencing some intermittent stumbling, exhaust backfires, and stalling lately, mainly when giving it gas after coming to a dead stop or occasionally when driving at a low speed (20-35 mph or so).  I got stranded twice today (!) when the car died (once at idle, once upon takeoff.)   Both times, I had to sit around for a half hour or so before it would finally fire back up.  It cranks fine, just won't turn over until some time passes.  (I'm guessing that I have to allow time for fuel line pressure to reduce and clear out some crud.) Luckily, I was able to limp on home.  Except for the 'occasional' stumbling, stalling, and backfires, the car's running fine and I'm getting no codes at all.  I can hear the fuel pump cycle on and off and the fuel pump relay click off (it's practically brand new, anyway.)  I've just recently put on new plugs, plug wires, O2 sensor, rotor, dist cap, PCV, EGR valve, and EGR solenoid.  All other sensors check out okay on the OBD scantool, FWIW.  I'm thinking (hoping) that my fuel filter is just clogged and needs replacing, or second, that possibly my fuel pump's going.  I haven't checked the fuel pressure yet...no gauge.  What do you think?  Am I barking up the right tree here?  Any help would be very much appreciated!  <P>Thanks,<BR>Stan <p>[This message has been edited by Stan86SE (edited 02-26-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||02-26-2001||09:58 PM||||Could very well your ignition module getting ready to die. A new fuel filter is always a good idea.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||02-26-2001||10:02 PM||||Timing chain and/or vacumn leaks (both?)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Stan86SE||02-26-2001||10:15 PM||||Thanks for the replies, guys!  What seems like a clue to me is that it will start back up again after stalling if I just give it some time to sit awhile first.  Does that point to anything in particular, you think?  Also, it's not overheating at all before it stalls.<P>Thanks,<BR>Stan <p>[This message has been edited by Stan86SE (edited 02-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||02-27-2001||05:45 AM||||Ignition module. Replace that and I'm pretty sure your problems will be over.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Stan86SE||02-27-2001||11:53 AM||||Thanks, Cliff.  Well, that's 2 for the ignition module.  I'll pick one up and see if things clear up.  Indiana, I've been searching for any vacuum leaks lately, but so far, so good.  Thanks again, all.||||reg||1
Z||000006||87GTZ34||02-27-2001||08:28 PM||||I 3rd the ignition module vote.  That is exactly how they go.  Lulling you into taking the car one more time until BAM!!! Right where you least want the thing to go completely, it does.  Pushing it up a hill or something....  Of course if that doesn't fix it, I once had the wire connector that goes from the distributor to the coil go.  It had an internal short with no break in the plastic casing.  It was had to find too as when you took it off to ohm it out, it would check out.  Put in back in, get it hot and let the vibration start on it, and the car would stumble.<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 02-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Stan86SE||02-27-2001||09:19 PM||||You've got that right, 87GTZ34.  I've been scared to take it out lately, thinking that the next time it stalled might be the last and then it wouldn't start back up, no matter how long I waited.  Not to mention the possibility of a stall at the worst possible time or place.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  I think I'll be able to get the ignition module and install it on Friday (3 days from now).  Hopefully, that'll do the trick.  It sure would be nice to be able to trust the ol' Fiero again and get back to just enjoying driving it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Stan86SE||02-27-2001||09:23 PM||||Btw, Cliff - _Fantastic_ site you've got here!  I feel very lucky to have found this forum and to be a member!<P>- Stan<BR>||||reg||1
